.TH tulayout n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tulayout
.PP
Page layout helpers for document block designers and renderers. Pure Tcl, no dependencies. Coordinates are in millimetres with origin at the top\-left of the page.
.SS API
.CS
tulayout::pageSize paper ?portrait|landscape?   ;# -> {widthMm heightMm}
tulayout::mmToPx mm scale
tulayout::pxToMm px scale
tulayout::snap mm ?-grid 5?
tulayout::isAutoY block                         ;# y==0 or lockedY
tulayout::normalizeBlock block ?-defaults dict?
tulayout::validateBlocks blocks                   ;# id -> block dict
tulayout::ensureBlocks blocks definitions         ;# fill missing ids
tulayout::blockOrder blocks ?definitions?
tulayout::blockRect block ?-height mm?
tulayout::mergeBlocks base preset ?-keys {x y w show}?
tulayout::mergeLayout target preset ?-keys {x y w show}?
tulayout::fitScale pageWmm pageHmm viewWpx viewHpx ?-marginPx 20?
tulayout::defaultBlockKeys
.CE
.SS "Block dict"
.PP
Each block is a dict. Common keys:
.TS
l l.
Key	Meaning
\fBlabel\fR	Human label in the designer
\fBx\fR, \fBy\fR, \fBw\fR, \fBh\fR	Position/size in mm
\fBshow\fR	\fB1\fR visible, \fB0\fR hidden
\fBlockedY\fR	\fB1\fR = auto vertical placement (\fBy\fR stays \fB0\fR)
.TE
.PP
\fBmergeBlocks\fR copies only the keys listed in \fB\-keys\fR (default \fB{x y w show}\fR) from \fBpreset\fR into \fBbase\fR for matching block ids. This is the usual “apply layout preset to a live document” operation.
.PP
\fBmergeLayout\fR expects full layout dicts with a \fBblocks\fR sub\-dict:
.CS
set doc [tulayout::mergeLayout $doc $preset]
.CE
.SS Papers
.PP
Supported names: \fBa4\fR, \fBa5\fR, \fBletter\fR. Unknown paper raises \fB{TCLUTILS TULAYOUT PAPER}\fR.
.SS Example
.CS
package require tclutils::tulayout

set blocks {
    header {label Header x 20 y 30 w 170 h 15 show 1}
    table  {label Table  x 20 y 0  w 170 h 40 show 1}
}
set preset {
    header {x 25 show 1}
}
set merged [tulayout::mergeBlocks $blocks $preset]
.CE
.SS Tests
.CS
tclsh tests/tulayout.test
tclsh examples/demo-tulayout.tcl
.CE
.SS "See also"
.PP
\fBtkutils::tkulayoutcanvas\fR — Tk megawidget built on this engine.
